From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 188/488] soh: rename func_800A6394 -> Skin_DrawArg6

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: fourth Skin_DrawImpl wrapper; like its siblings it is named for the parameter it adds over the previous one, but arg6's meaning is still unidentified so the name describes the signature, not the behaviour.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_skin.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 soh/include/functions.h | 2 +-
 soh/src/code/z_skin.c   | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/include/functions.h b/soh/include/functions.h
index b4a484b65..7aed0bec3 100644
--- a/soh/include/functions.h
+++ b/soh/include/functions.h
@@ -1355,7 +1355,7 @@ void Skin_DrawAnimatedLimb(GraphicsContext* gfxCtx, Skin* skin, s32 limbIndex, s
